You failed, but I'm a better hunter than you.

275
00:23:35,230 --> 00:23:36,410
Now...

276
00:23:37,810 --> 00:23:39,640
how about your little finger?

277
00:23:39,750 --> 00:23:41,420
You don't use that for much, do you?

278
00:23:41,430 --> 00:23:43,820
No? Good. Let's start with that.

279
00:23:54,480 --> 00:23:57,030
You've been wondering why you're here.

280
00:23:57,030 --> 00:23:58,220
Haven't you?

281
00:23:59,640 --> 00:24:01,310
Where you are.

282
00:24:01,830 --> 00:24:03,180
Who I am.

283
00:24:03,190 --> 00:24:05,370
Why I'm doing this to you.

284
00:24:07,390 --> 00:24:08,810
So guess.

285
00:24:09,950 --> 00:24:11,570
If you guess right,

286
00:24:11,800 --> 00:24:13,120
I'll tell you.

287
00:24:13,120 --> 00:24:16,220
By the old gods and the new, I swear it.

288
00:24:18,490 --> 00:24:19,910
You win the game

289
00:24:19,920 --> 00:24:22,070
if you can figure out who I am

290
00:24:22,070 --> 00:24:23,750
and why I'm torturing you

291
00:24:23,750 --> 00:24:26,980
and I win the game if you beg me to cut off your finger.

292
00:24:29,200 --> 00:24:32,190
If I win, you'll let me go?

293
00:24:34,920 --> 00:24:37,450
If you think this has a happy ending,

294
00:24:37,690 --> 00:24:40,170
you haven't been paying attention.

295
00:24:40,710 --> 00:24:41,740
Please.

296
00:24:42,490 --> 00:24:45,560
You say please again and you'll wish you hadn't.

297
00:24:49,740 --> 00:24:51,030
You first.

298
00:24:52,120 --> 00:24:53,290
Where are we?

299
00:24:55,080 --> 00:24:57,810
- The North. - Too vague.

300
00:24:57,810 --> 00:24:59,340
Deepwood Motte.

301
00:25:01,590 --> 00:25:03,500
Terrible guess.

302
00:25:11,430 --> 00:25:13,420
Now, where?

303
00:25:14,820 --> 00:25:16,330
Last Hearth.

304
00:25:16,700 --> 00:25:19,590
Do I look like a fucking Umber to you?

305
00:25:23,290 --> 00:25:24,760
Karhold!

306
00:25:32,130 --> 00:25:33,510
Karhold?

307
00:25:36,720 --> 00:25:38,240
How did you know that?

308
00:25:40,390 --> 00:25:43,130
Did you see any banners flying when we came in?

309
00:25:43,260 --> 00:25:44,380
No.

310
00:25:44,820 --> 00:25:46,520
It was just a guess.

311
00:25:47,890 --> 00:25:50,760
Very good, Lord Theon.

312
00:25:53,490 --> 00:25:54,850
And who am I?

313
00:25:55,940 --> 00:25:57,780
Torrhen Karstark.

314
00:25:57,970 --> 00:25:59,260
He's dead.

315
00:25:59,780 --> 00:26:02,550
Strangled by the Kingslayer.

316
00:26:04,610 --> 00:26:06,280
He was your brother.

317
00:26:11,610 --> 00:26:15,200
Your father is Lord Rickard Karstark.

318
00:26:24,270 --> 00:26:27,090
- You swore to tell me if I-- - You're right.

319
00:26:28,970 --> 00:26:32,590
Lord Rickard Karstark is Robb Stark's bannerman.

320
00:26:33,240 --> 00:26:34,940
I betrayed Robb.

321
00:26:35,970 --> 00:26:38,610
That's why you're torturing me.

322
00:26:41,150 --> 00:26:42,200
Yes.

323
00:26:46,180 --> 00:26:47,390
You win.

324
00:26:58,660 --> 00:27:01,740
Of course, you forgot to ask one question.

325
00:27:02,040 --> 00:27:04,230
You forgot to ask if I'm a liar.

326
00:27:10,950 --> 00:27:13,000
I'm afraid I am.

327
00:27:16,170 --> 00:27:18,900
Everything I told you is a lie.

328
00:27:21,630 --> 00:27:24,390
This isn't happening to you for a reason.

329
00:27:24,390 --> 00:27:28,610
Well, one reason-- I enjoy it.

330
00:27:28,610 --> 00:27:31,180
Please, cut it off! Cut it off! Cut it off!

331
00:27:37,770 --> 00:27:38,780
I win.

332
00:27:39,620 --> 00:27:41,580
Thank you for riding here so quickly.

333
00:27:42,230 --> 00:27:44,360
I know travel isn't easy in these times.

334
00:27:44,540 --> 00:27:46,970
The roads are crawling with cutthroats and bandits.

335
00:27:47,230 --> 00:27:50,430
But when the King of the North summons us, we come.

336
00:27:50,690 --> 00:27:52,980
Our father has instructed us to tell you

337
00:27:52,980 --> 00:27:55,610
that his alliance with the North can continue

338
00:27:56,260 --> 00:27:57,740
if his terms are met.

339
00:27:58,770 --> 00:28:01,210
Lord Frey requires a formal apology

340
00:28:01,420 --> 00:28:03,470
for your violation of your sacred oath

341
00:28:03,650 --> 00:28:05,150
to marry one of his daughters.

342
00:28:05,150 --> 00:28:07,730
Of course. He deserves as much. I was in the wrong.

343
00:28:07,930 --> 00:28:10,110
As restitution for this betrayal,

344
00:28:10,640 --> 00:28:13,570
he demands Harrenhal and all its attendant lands.

345
00:28:13,890 --> 00:28:16,230
- I don't think that's-- - We are fighting for the North.

346
00:28:17,970 --> 00:28:19,810
Harrenhal is not in the North.

347
00:28:20,400 --> 00:28:23,260
It is his once the war is over

348
00:28:23,870 --> 00:28:26,210
and we have no further strategic need for it.

349
00:28:27,530 --> 00:28:29,060
And there's something else.

350
00:28:29,860 --> 00:28:32,780
We will do whatever we can to give Lord Frey what he needs.

351
00:28:32,780 --> 00:28:36,040
Not what, whom.

352
00:28:38,770 --> 00:28:39,600
What?

353
00:28:46,160 --> 00:28:46,990
No.

354
00:28:47,230 --> 00:28:49,390
Our father requires Lord Edmure to wed

355
00:28:49,390 --> 00:28:51,980
one of his daughters-- Roslin.

356
00:28:52,280 --> 00:28:53,270
How old is she?

357
00:28:53,440 --> 00:28:54,250
19.

358
00:28:54,570 --> 00:28:55,630
Could I see her first?

359
00:28:55,630 --> 00:28:57,030
You want to count her teeth?

360
00:28:58,020 --> 00:28:59,890
We depart for the Twins in the morning.

361
00:29:00,390 --> 00:29:02,000
We need an answer before we leave

362
00:29:02,160 --> 00:29:03,850
and a wedding not more than a fortnight thereafter

363
00:29:03,850 --> 00:29:05,470
or this alliance is at an end.

364
00:29:05,470 --> 00:29:08,350
Your father does realize we're in the middle of a war?

365
00:29:08,970 --> 00:29:10,860
Father is old.

366
00:29:11,700 --> 00:29:13,170
It will put his heart at peace

367
00:29:13,170 --> 00:29:15,290
if he could see her wed to a good husband.

368
00:29:16,430 --> 00:29:20,560
And his recent experience has made him wary of long engagements.

369
00:29:21,220 --> 00:29:22,630
He has every right to be.

370
00:29:23,850 --> 00:29:25,750
Please excuse us while we discuss it.

371
00:29:42,880 --> 00:29:45,880
Why should I let that old ferret choose my bride for me?

372
00:29:46,320 --> 00:29:49,220
At the very least, I should be offered the same choice you were.

373
00:29:49,400 --> 00:29:50,660
I'm his liege lord.

374
00:29:50,820 --> 00:29:53,080
He's a proud man and we've wounded him.

375
00:29:53,080 --> 00:29:54,160
I didn't wound him.

376
00:29:55,090 --> 00:29:56,390
My answer is no.

377
00:30:00,920 --> 00:30:02,080
Listen to me

378
00:30:02,690 --> 00:30:05,520
and listen very carefully. You--

379
00:30:05,520 --> 00:30:08,180
The laws of gods and men are very clear.

380
00:30:08,620 --> 00:30:11,030
No man can compel another man to marry.

381
00:30:11,030 --> 00:30:13,330
The laws of my fist are about to compel your teeth.

382
00:30:13,330 --> 00:30:15,300
It's all right. You heard him.

383
00:30:16,900 --> 00:30:19,560
If you refuse, our alliance with the Freys is dead.

384
00:30:20,450 --> 00:30:23,310
He's wanted me for one of his daughters since I was 12.

385
00:30:23,510 --> 00:30:25,310
He's not gonna stop wanting it now.

386
00:30:26,440 --> 00:30:28,660
When I say no, he will come back

387
00:30:28,660 --> 00:30:30,570
and offer me a daughter of my choosing.

388
00:30:30,570 --> 00:30:32,540
You're willing to risk our freedom

389
00:30:32,540 --> 00:30:34,950
and our lives for a chance at a prettier wife?

390
00:30:34,950 --> 00:30:36,990
I have a war to fight.

391
00:30:37,590 --> 00:30:39,050
We can't win it without them.

392
00:30:39,300 --> 00:30:40,770
I have no time to haggle.

393
00:30:41,480 --> 00:30:43,580
You said you wanted to make amends for the Stone Mill.

394
00:30:44,370 --> 00:30:47,300
You recall that heroic engagement?

395
00:30:50,960 --> 00:30:54,520
I had something less permanent in mind.

396
00:30:54,930 --> 00:30:56,200
I've won every battle,

397
00:30:56,980 --> 00:30:58,590
but I'm losing this war.

398
00:31:00,650 --> 00:31:02,330
If we don't do this and do it now,

399
00:31:03,640 --> 00:31:04,750
we're lost.

400
00:31:11,300 --> 00:31:12,490
I'll marry her.

401
00:31:13,500 --> 00:31:15,250
You're paying for my sins, Uncle.

402
00:31:16,290 --> 00:31:17,830
It's not fair or right.

403
00:31:18,750 --> 00:31:20,250
I'll remember it.

404
00:31:26,610 --> 00:31:30,030
I see my men have finally found you something appropriate to wear.

405
00:31:30,630 --> 00:31:33,000
Yes. Most kind of them.

406
00:31:34,300 --> 00:31:36,420
You're a Stark bannerman, Lord Bolton.

407
00:31:36,600 --> 00:31:38,900
I am acting on Lady Stark's orders

408
00:31:38,900 --> 00:31:41,410
to return Jaime Lannister to King's Landing.

409
00:31:41,410 --> 00:31:44,380
When King Robb left Harrenhal, his mother was his prisoner.

410
00:31:45,040 --> 00:31:46,190
If she wasn't his mother,

411
00:31:46,190 --> 00:31:47,760
he'd have hanged her for treason.

412
00:31:55,820 --> 00:31:58,160
I should send you back to Robb Stark.

413
00:31:58,450 --> 00:31:59,800
You should.

414
00:32:00,600 --> 00:32:04,530
But instead, you're sitting here watching me fail at dinner.

415
00:32:05,630 --> 00:32:06,910
Why might that be?

416
00:32:07,370 --> 00:32:08,700
Wars cost money.

417
00:32:09,550 --> 00:32:11,810
Many people would pay a great deal for you.

418
00:32:12,010 --> 00:32:13,870
We both know who would pay the most.

419
00:32:15,840 --> 00:32:19,070
Or make you pay the most if he found out you had captured me

420
00:32:19,070 --> 00:32:21,430
and sent me back up north for a summary execution.

421
00:32:21,610 --> 00:32:22,650
You're right.

422
00:32:24,040 --> 00:32:25,310
Perhaps the safest thing to

423
00:32:25,310 --> 00:32:27,910
do is to kill you both and burn your bodies.

424
00:32:28,100 --> 00:32:29,180
It would be,

425
00:32:29,710 --> 00:32:32,840
if you honestly believed my father would never find out about it.

426
00:32:32,840 --> 00:32:35,220
King Robb is keeping your father quite busy.

427
00:32:35,650 --> 00:32:37,570
He doesn't have time for anything else.

428
00:32:37,950 --> 00:32:39,300
He'll make time for you.

429
00:32:43,490 --> 00:32:45,400
As soon as you're well enough to travel,

430
00:32:45,400 --> 00:32:47,850
I will allow you to go to King's Landing

431
00:32:47,850 --> 00:32:50,990
as restitution for the mistakes my soldiers made.

432
00:32:51,730 --> 00:32:54,420
And you will swear to tell your father the truth,

433
00:32:54,860 --> 00:32:57,030
that I had nothing to do with your maiming.

434
00:33:04,330 --> 00:33:06,320
- Shall we drink on it? - I don't partake.

435
00:33:08,630 --> 00:33:12,100
You do understand how suspicious that is to ordinary people?

436
00:33:13,980 --> 00:33:14,740
Very well.

437
00:33:16,020 --> 00:33:16,940
My lady,

438
00:33:18,000 --> 00:33:21,160
may our journey continue without further incident.

439
00:33:21,360 --> 00:33:22,960
Oh, she won't be going with you.

440
00:33:23,370 --> 00:33:25,560
I am charged with bringing Ser Jaime to--

441
00:33:25,560 --> 00:33:27,750
You are charged with abetting treason.

442
00:33:28,540 --> 00:33:30,420
I'm afraid I must insist.

443
00:33:30,870 --> 00:33:32,990
You're in no place to insist on anything.

444
00:33:33,740 --> 00:33:35,370
I would have hoped you'd learned your lesson

445
00:33:35,370 --> 00:33:38,770
about overplaying your position.

446
00:33:43,250 --> 00:33:45,000
- Impossible. - Why?

447
00:33:45,000 --> 00:33:47,630
My grandson is the pride of Highgarden.

448
00:33:47,820 --> 00:33:51,240
The most desirable bachelor in all seven kingdoms.

449
00:33:51,670 --> 00:33:53,690
- Your daughter-- - Is rich,

450
00:33:53,890 --> 00:33:56,790
the most beautiful woman in all seven kingdoms...

451
00:33:58,990 --> 00:34:00,330
and the mother of the king.

452
00:34:00,330 --> 00:34:01,610
Old.

453
00:34:02,660 --> 00:34:05,860
- Old? - Old.

454
00:34:06,720 --> 00:34:08,960
I'm something of an expert on the subject.

455
00:34:09,540 --> 00:34:11,860
Her change will be upon her before long.

456
00:34:12,040 --> 00:34:14,880
I'll spare you the details of what will happen then.

457
00:34:15,500 --> 00:34:18,030
You men may have a stomach for bloodshed and slaughter,

458
00:34:18,030 --> 00:34:20,250
but this is another matter entirely.

459
00:34:20,900 --> 00:34:23,570
The years punish us as well, I promise you that.

460
00:34:26,550 --> 00:34:30,320
My stomach remains quite strong, however.

461
00:34:31,100 --> 00:34:32,690
The only thing that might turn it

462
00:34:32,690 --> 00:34:36,170
are details of your grandson's nocturnal activities.

463
00:34:37,530 --> 00:34:39,460
- Do you deny them? - Oh, not at all.

464
00:34:39,880 --> 00:34:41,480
A sword swallower through and through.

465
00:34:41,900 --> 00:34:45,260
And a boy with his affliction should be grateful for the opportunity

466
00:34:45,260 --> 00:34:47,840
to marry the most beautiful woman in the kingdoms

467
00:34:48,020 --> 00:34:50,470
and remove the stain from his name.

468
00:34:50,470 --> 00:34:53,140
Did you grow up with boy cousins, Lord Tywin?

469
00:34:53,680 --> 00:34:55,560
Sons of your father's bannermen,

470
00:34:55,560 --> 00:34:57,790
squires, stable boys?

471
00:34:57,790 --> 00:34:59,060
Of course.

472
00:34:59,720 --> 00:35:02,380
And you never...

473
00:35:04,000 --> 00:35:04,920
No.

474
00:35:05,840 --> 00:35:06,940
Not once?

475
00:35:07,410 --> 00:35:08,800
Not in any way?

476
00:35:09,420 --> 00:35:10,400
Never.

477
00:35:10,930 --> 00:35:13,200
I congratulate you upon your restraint.

478
00:35:13,600 --> 00:35:15,800
But it's a natural thing, two boys having a go

479
00:35:15,800 --> 00:35:17,380
at each other beneath the sheets.

480
00:35:17,380 --> 00:35:20,190
Perhaps Highgarden has a high tolerance

481
00:35:20,190 --> 00:35:22,260
for unnatural behavior.

482
00:35:22,310 --> 00:35:23,720
I wouldn't say that.

483
00:35:23,920 --> 00:35:25,920
True, we don't tie ourselves in knots

484
00:35:25,920 --> 00:35:28,510
over a discreet bit of buggery, but...

485
00:35:30,700 --> 00:35:32,630
brothers and sisters--

486
00:35:34,430 --> 00:35:35,500
where I come from,

487
00:35:35,600 --> 00:35:39,170
that stain would be very difficult to wash out.

488
00:35:39,370 --> 00:35:41,450
I will not breathe further life

489
00:35:41,450 --> 00:35:43,930
into a malicious lie by discussing it.

490
00:35:46,100 --> 00:35:47,380
Lie or not,

491
00:35:47,560 --> 00:35:50,560
you must admit many people find it quite convincing.

492
00:35:50,950 --> 00:35:53,390
Convincing enough to put swords in their hands

493
00:35:53,390 --> 00:35:55,310
and send them off to kill Lannisters

494
00:35:55,310 --> 00:35:58,780
and Tyrells thanks to our new affiliation.

495
00:35:58,780 --> 00:36:00,650
I don't care what people believe.

496
00:36:01,340 --> 00:36:03,560
And neither do you.

497
00:36:04,240 --> 00:36:07,290
As an authority on myself, I must disagree.

498
00:36:08,120 --> 00:36:11,070
Now, if the rumors about my children were true,

499
00:36:11,630 --> 00:36:13,940
then Joffrey is no king at all

500
00:36:14,390 --> 00:36:18,560
and House Tyrell is throwing its prized flower into the dirt.

501
00:36:18,560 --> 00:36:21,910
And if Cersei is too old to give Loras children,

502
00:36:22,320 --> 00:36:26,110
we're throwing another prized flower into the dirt.

503
00:36:26,660 --> 00:36:29,240
It is a chance we simply cannot take.

504
00:36:30,150 --> 00:36:32,590
The uncertainty makes you uncomfortable.

505
00:36:33,870 --> 00:36:34,930
All right.

506
00:36:35,860 --> 00:36:37,590
I'll remove it for you.

507
00:36:38,390 --> 00:36:41,500
If you refuse to marry Loras to Cersei,

508
00:36:41,960 --> 00:36:44,290
I will name him to the Kingsguard.

509
00:36:45,010 --> 00:36:47,790
I'm sure you're familiar with the Kingsguard vows.

510
00:36:47,980 --> 00:36:49,400
He will never marry.

511
00:36:49,590 --> 00:36:51,450
He will never have children.

512
00:36:51,450 --> 00:36:53,540
The Tyrell name will fade.

513
00:36:54,080 --> 00:36:57,840
And Highgarden will go to the children of Joffrey and Margaery.

514
00:36:57,840 --> 00:37:00,170
You would have your grandson protected

515
00:37:00,170 --> 00:37:02,210
by someone who disgusts you?

516
00:37:02,210 --> 00:37:05,270
I would have my grandson protected by a skilled warrior

517
00:37:05,960 --> 00:37:08,370
who takes his vows seriously.

518
00:37:09,150 --> 00:37:11,890
So, shall I draw up the order?

519
00:37:13,470 --> 00:37:16,090
Or do you consent to this marriage?

520
00:37:20,610 --> 00:37:22,290
It's a rare enough thing --

521
00:37:23,340 --> 00:37:26,530
a man who lives up to his reputation.

522
00:38:19,090 --> 00:38:20,040
No!

523
00:38:40,250 --> 00:38:42,070
We've gotta cut them loose!

524
00:38:42,360 --> 00:38:43,500
No!

525
00:39:29,830 --> 00:39:31,410
Take my hand!

526
00:40:07,430 --> 00:40:08,940
That's a wonderful pin.

527
00:40:11,380 --> 00:40:13,170
Oh, it's more of a brooch, really.

528
00:40:16,560 --> 00:40:19,110
Though I suppose a brooch is a sort of pin, so...

529
00:40:24,920 --> 00:40:27,730
I'm very happy about...

530
00:40:28,620 --> 00:40:30,150
Uh, yes.

531
00:40:31,090 --> 00:40:32,380
I-I am as well.

532
00:40:34,980 --> 00:40:36,710
I feel like I'm in a dream.

533
00:40:37,090 --> 00:40:39,150
Yes, me, too. Definitely.

534
00:40:40,710 --> 00:40:43,180
I've dreamed of a large wedding since I was quite young.

535
00:40:43,630 --> 00:40:46,900
The guests, the food, the tournaments.

536
00:40:50,890 --> 00:40:53,020
And the bride, of course.

537
00:40:57,140 --> 00:40:59,080
The most beautiful bride in the world

538
00:40:59,880 --> 00:41:01,460
in a beautiful gown of gold

539
00:41:01,460 --> 00:41:03,850
and green brocade with fringed sleeves.

540
00:41:06,440 --> 00:41:08,250
Have you ever been to Highgarden, my lady?

541
00:41:09,450 --> 00:41:13,170
No. I had never left Winterfell before I came to King's Landing.

542
00:41:14,460 --> 00:41:15,890
But it sounds wonderful.

543
00:41:15,890 --> 00:41:17,490
I can't wait to see it.

544
00:41:18,790 --> 00:41:20,990
And to leave this place.

545
00:41:21,910 --> 00:41:23,100
It's terrible, isn't it?

546
00:41:26,400 --> 00:41:28,370
The most terrible place there is.

547
00:41:38,260 --> 00:41:41,490
I don't suppose there's anything we can do about this.

548
00:41:41,710 --> 00:41:43,190
We can have them both killed.

549
00:41:45,680 --> 00:41:47,340
It's hard to say which of the four of us

550
00:41:47,340 --> 00:41:49,380
is getting the worst of this arrangement.

551
00:41:50,430 --> 00:41:51,850
Probably Sansa.

552
00:41:52,480 --> 00:41:54,420
Though Loras will certainly come to know

553
00:41:54,420 --> 00:41:56,460
a deep and singular misery.

554
00:41:57,310 --> 00:41:59,020
Father doesn't discriminate.

555
00:42:00,030 --> 00:42:02,490
We're all being shipped off to hell together.

556
00:42:03,310 --> 00:42:04,880
On a boat you built.

557
00:42:05,780 --> 00:42:07,680
The Tyrells were plotting to undermine our family.

558
00:42:07,680 --> 00:42:10,560
I did what I did to protect our family.

559
00:42:10,560 --> 00:42:11,990
I'm your family.

560
00:42:13,640 --> 00:42:15,420
A member of your family

561
00:42:15,420 --> 00:42:18,520
who has actively contributed to that family's survival.

562
00:42:19,800 --> 00:42:21,660
Whether or not you or Father

563
00:42:21,660 --> 00:42:23,470
or anyone else wants to admit it.

564
00:42:23,470 --> 00:42:24,600
I do admit it.

565
00:42:26,140 --> 00:42:28,190
If it weren't for your trick with the wildfire,

566
00:42:28,830 --> 00:42:31,720
Stannis would have sacked the city before Father got here.

567
00:42:32,860 --> 00:42:35,190
Our heads would still be rotting on the city gate.

568
00:42:35,350 --> 00:42:39,030
Trying to have me killed is an odd way of saying thank you.

569
00:42:41,820 --> 00:42:43,590
There are two people in King's Landing

570
00:42:43,590 --> 00:42:45,480
who can give an order to a Kingsguard.

571
00:42:46,030 --> 00:42:49,150
Did you or did you not order Ser Mandon

572
00:42:49,150 --> 00:42:51,520
to kill me during the Battle of the Blackwater?

573
00:43:01,580 --> 00:43:03,410
The impulse I understand.

574
00:43:05,230 --> 00:43:08,030
He hates me because I'm the only one

575
00:43:08,030 --> 00:43:10,900
who tells him what he really is.

576
00:43:14,530 --> 00:43:17,650
So, fair enough. He wants me dead.

577
00:43:18,540 --> 00:43:20,190
But his stupidity?

578
00:43:20,940 --> 00:43:23,380
He could have had me poisoned and no one would have known.

579
00:43:24,430 --> 00:43:27,770
But the king orders a Kingsguard

580
00:43:27,770 --> 00:43:29,800
to murder the Hand of the King

581
00:43:29,970 --> 00:43:31,800
in full view of his own army.

582
00:43:31,800 --> 00:43:33,280
The boy's an idiot.

583
00:43:33,700 --> 00:43:35,080
What do you want me to say?

584
00:43:35,080 --> 00:43:37,780
I want you to tell me if my life is still in danger.

585
00:43:37,780 --> 00:43:38,770
Probably.

586
00:43:40,370 --> 00:43:41,450
But not from Joffrey.

587
00:43:41,450 --> 00:43:43,300
He won't do anything now Father's here.

588
00:43:45,280 --> 00:43:47,640
Seven kingdoms united in fear

589
00:43:47,640 --> 00:43:49,390
of Tywin Lannister.

590
00:43:50,090 --> 00:43:51,320
Not the Tyrells.

591
00:43:52,250 --> 00:43:54,110
Soon they won't need to be afraid of him.

592
00:43:54,600 --> 00:43:55,920
Joffrey will belong to Margaery,

593
00:43:55,920 --> 00:43:57,480
the little doe-eyed whore.

594
00:43:58,120 --> 00:44:00,210
And so will his children and their children.

595
00:44:01,030 --> 00:44:03,050
History will be taken from our hands.

596
00:44:05,320 --> 00:44:06,990
You may escape, at least.

597
00:44:08,030 --> 00:44:09,520
Once Jaime gets back,

598
00:44:09,520 --> 00:44:13,670
Ser Loras may come down with a terrible case of sword through bowels.

599
00:44:15,220 --> 00:44:16,920
When Jaime gets back, yes.

600
00:44:17,480 --> 00:44:18,780
But when do we think that's going to be?

601
00:44:18,780 --> 00:44:20,460
He's out there somewhere.

602
00:44:22,620 --> 00:44:26,190
Jaime or not, I'm truly fucked.

603
00:44:29,650 --> 00:44:31,160
Who's going to tell her?

604
00:44:33,300 --> 00:44:35,450
Do you think people will like it?

605
00:44:35,650 --> 00:44:37,880
I don't think they will even notice it.

606
00:44:37,880 --> 00:44:40,400
You're right. It's not my wedding.

607
00:44:41,930 --> 00:44:43,310
Anyway, from what I can tell,

608
00:44:43,310 --> 00:44:45,760
the dressmakers in Highgarden will be far superior

609
00:44:45,760 --> 00:44:47,380
to the ones in King's Landing.

610
00:44:47,560 --> 00:44:50,120
They'd never make me anything as dull as this for my wedding.

611
00:44:51,670 --> 00:44:53,740
Loras likes green and gold brocade.

612
00:44:54,600 --> 00:44:56,280
I'm sure he does.

613
00:44:57,890 --> 00:44:59,860
Will they let me invite my family?

614
00:45:00,320 --> 00:45:02,330
They haven't asked my opinion.

615
00:45:02,330 --> 00:45:03,780
But do you think they will?

616
00:45:04,780 --> 00:45:05,450
No.

617
00:45:13,290 --> 00:45:14,990
Lady Sansa, Lord Tyrion to see you.

618
00:45:14,990 --> 00:45:17,430
- Should I-- - I beg your pardon, my lady.

619
00:45:18,900 --> 00:45:20,080
Good afternoon, Lord Tyrion.

620
00:45:20,080 --> 00:45:22,410
I was just trying on a gown for King Joffrey's wedding.

621
00:45:24,160 --> 00:45:27,540
Yes, it should be quite a wedding.

622
00:45:28,770 --> 00:45:31,080
I need to speak with you, Lady Sansa.

623
00:45:31,570 --> 00:45:32,510
Of course.

624
00:45:33,630 --> 00:45:35,080
Alone, if I may.

625
00:45:35,450 --> 00:45:37,050
Why do you need to speak to her alone?

626
00:45:37,050 --> 00:45:37,890
Shae.

627
00:45:38,930 --> 00:45:40,380
Please excuse her, Lord Tyrion.

628
00:45:40,380 --> 00:45:41,560
She's not from here.

629
00:45:42,180 --> 00:45:43,410
But I trust her,

630
00:45:43,590 --> 00:45:45,290
even though she tells me not to.

631
00:45:47,770 --> 00:45:51,290
Sometimes we think we want to hear something

632
00:45:51,800 --> 00:45:54,010
and it's only afterwards when it's too late

633
00:45:54,010 --> 00:45:56,320
that we realize we wished we'd heard it

634
00:45:56,320 --> 00:45:59,390
under entirely different circumstances.

635
00:45:59,390 --> 00:46:00,800
It's all right, really.

636
00:46:04,890 --> 00:46:06,230
How to begin?

637
00:46:09,860 --> 00:46:11,020
It's-- this--

638
00:46:12,060 --> 00:46:15,180
this-- this is awkward.

639
00:46:17,920 --> 00:46:19,350
1,000 blades

640
00:46:19,980 --> 00:46:22,830
taken from the hands of Aegon's fallen enemies,

641
00:46:22,830 --> 00:46:26,320
forged in the fiery breath of Balerion the Dread.

642
00:46:26,320 --> 00:46:28,300
There aren't 1,000 blades.

643
00:46:29,410 --> 00:46:31,140
There aren't even 200.

644
00:46:32,330 --> 00:46:33,580
I've counted.

645
00:46:33,580 --> 00:46:35,540
Ha, I'm sure you have.

646
00:46:36,500 --> 00:46:38,160
Ugly old thing.

647
00:46:39,100 --> 00:46:41,420
Yet it has a certain appeal.

648
00:46:42,200 --> 00:46:44,390
The Lysa Arryn of chairs.

649
00:46:44,390 --> 00:46:47,100
Shame you had to settle for your second choice.

650
00:46:47,100 --> 00:46:49,280
Early days, my friend.

651
00:46:49,580 --> 00:46:51,830
It is flattering, really...

652
00:46:53,880 --> 00:46:56,450
you feeling such dread

653
00:46:56,450 --> 00:46:58,920
at the prospect of me getting what I want.

654
00:46:58,920 --> 00:47:01,780
Thwarting you has never been my primary ambition,

655
00:47:01,780 --> 00:47:02,870
I promise you.

656
00:47:03,620 --> 00:47:07,090
Although who doesn't like to see their friends fail now and then?

657
00:47:07,090 --> 00:47:08,330
You're so right.

658
00:47:08,680 --> 00:47:09,710
For instance,

659
00:47:10,310 --> 00:47:14,200
when I thwarted your plan to give Sansa Stark to the Tyrells.

660
00:47:14,200 --> 00:47:16,120
If I'm going to be honest,

661
00:47:16,120 --> 00:47:20,540
I did feel an unmistakable sense of enjoyment there.

662
00:47:21,930 --> 00:47:23,690
But your confidant,

663
00:47:24,440 --> 00:47:27,630
the one who fed you information about my plans,

664
00:47:28,000 --> 00:47:30,080
the one you swore to protect...

665
00:47:31,890 --> 00:47:33,990
you didn't bring her any enjoyment.

666
00:47:35,530 --> 00:47:37,980
And she didn't bring me any enjoyment.

667
00:47:39,370 --> 00:47:42,160
She was a bad investment on my part.

668
00:47:44,080 --> 00:47:47,060
Luckily, I have a friend

669
00:47:47,600 --> 00:47:49,690
who wanted to try something new.

670
00:47:50,420 --> 00:47:51,950
Something daring.

671
00:47:53,490 --> 00:47:56,830
And he was so grateful to me for providing

672
00:47:56,830 --> 00:47:59,850
this fresh experience.

673
00:48:04,550 --> 00:48:07,160
I did what I did for the good of the realm.

674
00:48:07,640 --> 00:48:08,630
The realm?

675
00:48:09,860 --> 00:48:11,730
Do you know what the realm is?

676
00:48:13,970 --> 00:48:17,120
It's the thousand blades of Aegon's enemies.

677
00:48:17,540 --> 00:48:22,130
A story we agree to tell each other over and over

678
00:48:22,520 --> 00:48:24,910
till we forget that it's a lie.

679
00:48:24,910 --> 00:48:28,730
But what do we have left once we abandon the lie?

680
00:48:29,460 --> 00:48:30,430
Chaos.

681
00:48:31,240 --> 00:48:33,690
A gaping pit waiting to swallow us all.

682
00:48:33,920 --> 00:48:36,580
Chaos isn't a pit.

683
00:48:37,770 --> 00:48:39,720
Chaos is a ladder.

684
00:48:42,070 --> 00:48:44,080
Many who try to climb it fail

685
00:48:44,720 --> 00:48:46,540
and never get to try again.

686
00:48:48,160 --> 00:48:50,240
The fall breaks them.

687
00:48:59,440 --> 00:49:02,730
And some are given a chance to climb,

688
00:49:03,160 --> 00:49:04,730
but they refuse.

689
00:49:05,850 --> 00:49:07,430
They cling to the realm

690
00:49:08,770 --> 00:49:10,220
or the gods

691
00:49:10,780 --> 00:49:11,950
or love.

692
00:49:13,490 --> 00:49:14,920
Illusions.

693
00:49:16,750 --> 00:49:18,700
Only the ladder is real.

694
00:49:19,560 --> 00:49:22,100
The climb is all there is.

